From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: skip the user-PD stop handshake when the firmware is gone

ath11k_ahb_stop_user_pd() always raises the SMP2P stop request and waits
ATH11K_USERPD_STOP_TIMEOUT for the ack of the firmware that spawned the user
PD. After a fatal error on the Q6 that firmware no longer exists: on this
tree the root PD restarts on its own (coredump disabled) but does not
respawn the user PDs, and ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH stays set until a
recovery brings the firmware back. The ack can never arrive, so the
watchdog's driver reload after a root-PD crash spends 5 s per radio in the
wait and logs "UserPD stop wait timed out" twice.

Skip the handshake while CRASH_FLUSH is set and power the radio down
directly. A healthy stop is unchanged: the flag is set on the
firmware-crash path (QMI server exit) and cleared once a recovery succeeds.

Measured on the RD03v2 bench (IPQ5018 + QCN6122), Q6 assert followed by the
watchdog's reload: both stop timeouts gone. This is the clean-tree form of
the change first tested on top of the private user-PD experiments (see
v2/candidates/private-userpd/).

Signed-off-by: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
@@ -510,6 +510,20 @@ static void ath11k_ahb_stop_user_pd(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 	struct ath11k_ahb *ab_ahb = ath11k_ahb_priv(ab);
 	unsigned long time_left;
 
+	/*
+	 * The stop request is an SMP2P handshake that the firmware which
+	 * spawned this user PD answers. After a fatal error on the Q6 that
+	 * firmware is gone (ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH stays set until a recovery
+	 * brings it back), and the root PD restarts without respawning the
+	 * user PDs, so nothing can ever ack: the wait would only burn its
+	 * timeout. Power the radio down without it.
+	 */
+	if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ab->dev_flags)) {
+		ath11k_info(ab, "UserPD%d: firmware gone, skipping the stop handshake\n",
+			    ab_ahb->userpd_id);
+		goto power_off;
+	}
+
 	qcom_smem_state_update_bits(ab_ahb->stop_state, BIT(ab_ahb->stop_bit),
 				    BIT(ab_ahb->stop_bit));
 
@@ -520,6 +534,7 @@ static void ath11k_ahb_stop_user_pd(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 
 	qcom_smem_state_update_bits(ab_ahb->stop_state, BIT(ab_ahb->stop_bit), 0);
 
+power_off:
 	if (ab->hw_rev == ATH11K_HW_IPQ5018_HW10)
 		qcom_scm_pas_set_wifi_power_mode(MPD_WCNSS_PAS_ID, false);
 }
